#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096456 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096669 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8f8937b-de15-5d4c-aa77-1d45595fc7af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "201a713a-83ca-5e31-9a4f-257795d7eb1b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4690" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n![](images/3b/3b7ca238880ce9b06f58b1667d29b3fa0103560fa475238134cd3e802c7e7720.png)" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 2-2 = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = 3-2 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1,$ $y=0,$ and $z = 2.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096457 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096670 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cc8ce97a-3bda-506f-b9d2-98ac7524583a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4691" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n![](images/1e/1ecadec01586fecee4a8b6d8ad5015168387124430849ed2e7d884908e28e927.png)" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n![](images/c7/c7c7d0904aa85c2cd9915e95a8ca3cee9857deb216148f59372204c6672d8811.png)\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096458 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/id #uuid "7b44089c-8ca7-57e5-b390-7900647e3884" :question/math-academy-id "e-4692" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n![](images/fd/fd5c0fe6de60e36b0bd2414cb8ef991265c30bdfa4d8cfdac3242f51a54dbb87.png)" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n![](images/41/41347eb5694181e386cae05a31e455d12e2fbd1a0d70cd36bb37ed72da75f82d.png)\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "517c2b95-3278-5288-97a8-8f4ad7d12b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-15,40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236335} {:answer/id #uuid "58b90198-a181-5ca7-820a-0cb2ae4ad41b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-85,40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236375} {:answer/id #uuid "782c23fb-f476-55a3-962b-c00da83d7887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-75,40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236570} {:answer/id #uuid "9af36a41-8158-5002-b336-bc334832f54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,-10,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236790} {:answer/id #uuid "b734756b-8742-55f6-b6ab-d04424db9104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-75,-10,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "782c23fb-f476-55a3-962b-c00da83d7887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-75,40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236570} :answer-field/id #uuid "746029b9-082c-5f33-9a0e-5b120cac1acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5592cf72-9e61-50b5-9aec-b1921100f3dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-10204" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=10 \\\\  & y+5z=15 \\\\  & -z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=5\\,⟹\\,z=-5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+5(-5)=15\\,⟹\\,y=15+25=40.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-5$ and $y=40$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(40)-(-5)=10\\,⟹\\,x=10-80-5=-75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-75,y=40$ and $z=-5.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-75,40,-5⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096670 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "182dccc5-8d2b-538a-83cd-6b89a3bfbad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235965} {:answer/id #uuid "3307379c-e700-51d9-9e99-3e3bd5ec477f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236139} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b17a9a-90d7-5870-b6b3-1af698f37d2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236938} {:answer/id #uuid "c0484c72-d9c5-5f37-a8a6-65ce5f234ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237040} {:answer/id #uuid "cfaecad6-9a62-5f87-a4c9-cc1014ce4d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfaecad6-9a62-5f87-a4c9-cc1014ce4d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237135} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a8b1db1-b5f2-508a-bbfc-19cbd8de4aba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aaed5b7a-0eac-529c-ad7e-d0cc31abe7a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-10205" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=1 \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=0$, and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,0,1⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096669 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8f8937b-de15-5d4c-aa77-1d45595fc7af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bb7eb03-f9e4-5c84-825e-4af3dc459a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263370} {:answer/id #uuid "3267cac5-e192-561d-abb2-9c349b094047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ -1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263433} {:answer/id #uuid "379c045a-17f7-55f6-b610-cc58a5bf28a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263502} {:answer/id #uuid "39fe00c8-2263-5a88-8044-ac8d9246b900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263517} {:answer/id #uuid "421302c0-ff7e-5cd9-98df-d7ad54cd1916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bb7eb03-f9e4-5c84-825e-4af3dc459a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263370} :answer-field/id #uuid "abadbea5-ec63-5456-93e5-7d951e9c42cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bdb97edb-fdd8-52f8-9de8-da5dc252cf96" :question/math-academy-id "q-129455" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}=3 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6(-\\frac{1}{3})=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3-2=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+1-(-\\frac{1}{3})=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2-1-\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{3}$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096670 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56c0707e-0631-5e99-ba02-7389b388e45b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-14,7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263750} {:answer/id #uuid "82adc88c-6f01-5181-9b3e-6079f1c14df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264124} {:answer/id #uuid "8f112d6e-e159-5a64-9f51-5168e778a6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-11,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264225} {:answer/id #uuid "a0bc6c5e-c56c-5847-ad25-ed2e38054f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-14,-7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264365} {:answer/id #uuid "e977e059-2220-541b-a75d-ec8440736b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e977e059-2220-541b-a75d-ec8440736b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-7,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265030} :answer-field/id #uuid "f834e889-235e-5ed6-b433-9cd676419b25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f98c00cd-fa7a-5960-9ffe-f0175b73e871" :question/math-academy-id "q-129599" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-1 \\\\  & y+3z=2 \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2-9=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-7)+2(3)=-1\\,⟹\\,x=-1+7-6=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=-7$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,-7,3⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165ea2fd-41c0-5400-b24b-77486a19a825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339326} {:answer/id #uuid "67ae6eb0-f860-56b5-a08f-2f5623a97b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340049} {:answer/id #uuid "bf55a7f8-3683-5adc-8cf6-442d5d29a568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340833} {:answer/id #uuid "ddecb468-7ba6-5116-8ff8-2b5e7fe02d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341099} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf0aed3-bba1-520d-802b-6e0413c2d5b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddecb468-7ba6-5116-8ff8-2b5e7fe02d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341099} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7e5e5a9-3bd5-5992-93ff-7ad964a75306" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41fa8809-57ef-578c-b39f-9d0b73e06f90" :question/math-academy-id "q-72981" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+z=2 \\\\  & 3y+2z=-1 \\\\  & -z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=2\\,⟹\\,z=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n3y+2(-2)=-1\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}(-1+4)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-2$ and $y=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,x=2+2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=1$, and $z=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
